sg-session (0.1.0-15) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Voice typing's engine: sg-dictate runs NVIDIA Parakeet TDT 0.6B v3 (int8
    ONNX) on the CPU with python3-onnxruntime and Silero VAD, captures from
    PipeWire, turns spoken punctuation into marks, drops filler words and
    writes numbers as digits, and serves sg-shell's dictation toolbar over a
    bridge. Nothing heard is stored or logged.
  * sg-speechd (socket-activated, root): downloads the speech model once per
    machine from pinned revisions, checked by SHA-256 and resumable, into
    /var/lib/stained-glass-speech, for anyone with a Windows session;
    removing it is an administrator's.
  * sg-run-explorer starts the hold-to-talk listener (sg-dictate /background).
  * Gates: test/dictate-test.py (in make lint) and make test-dictate (real
    speech through the real model).

